  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "If \\(x\\) cows give \\(x+1\\) cans of milk in \\(x+2\\) days, how many days will it take \\(x+3\\) cows to give \\(x+5\\) cans of milk?",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{x(x+2)(x+5)}{(x+1)(x+3)}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{x(x+1)(x+5)}{(x+2)(x+3)}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{(x+1)(x+3)(x+5)}{x(x+2)}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{(x+1)(x+3)}{x(x+2)(x+5)}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "none of these"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1976-p13.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The production rate is \\(\\frac{x+1}{x(x+2)}\\) cans per cow-day. If the new time is \\(T,\\) then \\[ \\frac{x+5}{(x+3)T}=\\frac{x+1}{x(x+2)}. \\] Hence \\(T=\\frac{x(x+2)(x+5)}{(x+1)(x+3)}.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "First find the number of cans produced per cow-day",
        "Set \\(\\frac{x+5}{(x+3)T}=\\frac{x+1}{x(x+2)}\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
